4): about 50 fewer units short per product. That gains about +260 on product 0 and about −97 on product 1, net of the extra purchases. But the average buffer grows by about 27 units per product, which adds about 1,050 in storage. Net: roughly −900 compared with 1.0×.\n   - Product 1 is expensive (buy 9, sell 14) and its shortage penalty is small (2), so over-ordering it is especially costly.\n   - At 1.2–1.25× (candidates 6 and 7) the losses are larger: surplus piles up and goes unsold.\n\n**Ranking:**\n- Candidate 5 (1.0×, every other day) is best. It ties candidate 0 on fees versus storage, and its two-day batches absorb demand swings slightly better.\n- Candidate 0 (1.0×, daily) is just behind.\n- Candidates 1 and 4 (1.1×) are worse. Candidate 4 also pays one extra order fee.\n- Candidate 3 (1.1×, daily) and candidate 2 (three-day batches) are worse again.\n- Candidates 6 and 7 are the worst."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 353, "cache_read_input_tokens": 5728, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 353}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-26T00:52:52.417Z", "request_id": "req_011CgPvxwkhMFoezZLTLNRtv"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01EGeihUaNpqDSscKr21Zaog", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgPvxx2KyEH3CjqbZm4Jt", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": 